codex
The first XCFramework passed static, architecture, min-OS, forbidden-symbol, module-map, and absolute-path checks across all three slices. I spotted one reproducibility weakness before locking it: OpenSSL’s configured install prefix was a random temp path, and Apple resolves temp paths through both `/var/folders` and `/private/var`; the existing path scanner covered only the latter. I’m fixing the recipe to embed a stable logical prefix and tightening the scanner before the two lock-comparison builds.
apply patch
