The tightened scanner did its job and rejected the candidate: OpenSSL records its full compiler option string, so the temporary path inside `-ffile-prefix-map=…` itself leaked even though source paths were remapped. OpenSSL already compiles relative source paths, so I’m removing that temp-valued flag only from OpenSSL; libssh2 keeps path remapping because CMake supplies absolute sources and does not expose its build flags at runtime.
